language-derived-from-the-record-5 = unlines (cons "**3. Context selects: a fiber.** For a participant i, a word w is the type Occ_i(w) of events of i's record that i identifies as w, its paths i's identifications, and each occurrence e has a context c(e) ∈ C, the record around it. At a moment t the present occurrence of w has context c_t. The selected occurrences are the fiber of the context map over it: Sel_i(w, t) = Σ_{e : Occ_i(w)} Path_C(c(e), c_t) = Fib_c(c_t). An occurrence is selected exactly when its context is identified with the present one: no weight, a path or none. Identifying contexts is identifying the occurrences they are made of, whose selection runs through their contexts in turn: paths between occurrences (the same word) inside paths between contexts (the same surroundings) inside paths between those. The record with its identifications is a higher type; selection is a fiber of it; meaning lives in the hypercubical path structure of the record, not at any one level." nil)
